      "date": "2026-07-27 20:08:50.000000000",
      "message": "Patch Set 3:\n\n(5 comments)\n\nAI code review results below, please doublecheck\n\nExperimental feature testing in progress, please pay attention to the comments\n\nSome concerns, see inline comments. The main one is that nothing pins the two writes into the same second, so the test can pass on a build without the i_version fix.\n\nAlso, the fix this covers touches both osc_lock.c and mdc_dev.c, but $TESTDIR is created with `setstripe -c -1`, so only the OSC cancellation path is exercised. Would a second file with a DoM layout (`$LFS setstripe -E 1M -L mdt`) be worth adding to cover mdc_dlm_canceling()?",
